cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Cite the archived DOI of
  the exact release you used (Zenodo–GitHub integration), and check the archive
  against its MANIFEST.sha256. The repository name carries "v3.3.0"; it is not
  a version identifier (RELEASE.md). The git history of E1/E2 (preregistration
  commits eb03ad2, 1905da1) lives in the original repository
  ASTRA-Unified-ResearchLab-MCP-FCS-v3.1.0 (empirical/PROVENANCE.md §2bis).
type: software
title: "ASTRA-FCS — Agent-orchestrated Simulation Testbed for Research on Access (MCP server, FCS layer)"
version: 3.3.0-rc.3
# date-released must equal the date of the signed tag v3.3.0-rc.3 (RELEASE.md §2); set it when tagging.
date-released: 2026-10-19
# Composite licensing: MIT for the original work; python/the_consciousness_ai/ and the
# nine ported files of src/engine/tcai/ follow the upstream NON-COMMERCIAL licence.
# No single SPDX identifier describes the whole, hence license-url (CFF 1.2.0).
license-url: "https://github.com/christophejlegros-lgtm/ASTRA-FCS-v3.3.0/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"
repository-code: "https://github.com/christophejlegros-lgtm/ASTRA-FCS-v3.3.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Legros
    given-names: Christophe Jean
    affiliation: "Assistance Multi IA, Geneva"
    email: Assistant-Multi-IA@proton.me
abstract: >-
  ASTRA-FCS is a research instrument for simulating and auditing functional
  correlates of access (Block 1995) under substrate constraints; it neither
  measures, detects nor attributes phenomenal consciousness. Model Context
  Protocol server exposing 75 simulation and analysis tools to AI
  assistants: a LIF+STDP spiking network, a JEPA-style world model, computed
  proxies named after theories of consciousness, simulated bridges to
  biocomputing platforms, an executable layer for the research programme of
  substrate-constrained functionalism (FCS), and a read-only functional-teleology
  extension (pre-release) that assesses declared purposes against reported
  outcome intervals under hard constraints. All biological and physiological
  data are simulated; the consciousness-related indices are proxies, not
  measurements, each documented by a proxy card and checked by validation
  controls (v3.2.0). Third-party components keep their own licences (see
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - spiking neural network
  - active inference
  - consciousness science
  - biocomputing
  - epistemology
